ng had about 1,173 counties. The totals fluctuated as boundaries were revised <br>5. CantonsMing counties were subdivided into half a dozen or more cantons <br>6. TownshipCantons were divided into about a dozen townships <br>7. WardsTownships were divided into dozen of wards. A ward was small enough- mandated as fifty families in the Yuan, a hundred or so families in the Ming- to conform the contours of existing villages, or that was ideal. \n                    '}], {'usage.total_tokens': 1278, 'usage.prompt_tokens': 1187})
